@@ -68,6 +68,24 @@ The wheel, from the top going clockwise: Danger, Push, On My Way, All In, Assist
 
 ## Settings
 
+### Ask your existing Codex / ChatGPT pet (Windows, local extension)
+
+Enable **Settings → Pings & sound → Ask your pet with a Need Vision ping**. Keep your existing desktop pet visible and signed in.
+Hold **Alt**, drag down-left to the green **Need Vision** icon on the default wheel, and release both the mouse and Alt. lolPing captures the display where
+the ping started, circles that point, and asks the pet what the marked item means. The reply appears in the pet's own
+activity bubble; click it to read the full answer. It uses your existing ChatGPT account and requires no API key.
+
+Only your own **Need Vision** pings send screenshots; `? / Enemy Missing` is a normal ping. Settings previews and room members' pings do not. The screenshot includes
+everything visible on the pinged display. Temporary capture files are removed after the handoff, while the image and
+question remain in the chat created by the pet. Existing pet drafts are preserved, and repeated pings during handoff
+are ignored. If the handoff fails, lolPing shows the reason; check the pet for a partial draft before retrying.
+
+This uses the documented **Windows + Alt + P** shortcut and ordinary Windows accessibility/keyboard input, so it
+depends on the pet UI and shortcut staying compatible. Tested with desktop version **26.928.4866.0**. It adds no
+replacement pet or answer window. An upstream lolPing update may replace this local extension.
+
+The Windows build also compiles `native/pet-bridge` using the .NET Framework compiler included with Windows.
+
 <img src="docs/media/settings.png" width="760" alt="The lolPing settings window, with sections for trigger, toggle, pings and sound, wheel, emotes, room and app">
 
 - **Trigger key:** Alt, Ctrl, Shift, Win, Caps Lock, Mouse 4, Mouse 5 or any other key (on a Mac: Option, Control, Shift, Command, Mouse 4, Mouse 5 or any other key). The custom key won't type in other apps while pinging is on.
